course: dictionary
lesson: 14466
title: Partially and partly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Partially means partly, or not completely. The word is closely linked to part, so think of a piece of something rather than the whole thing. «The jug was partially filled with water.» The jug is not empty and it is not full to the top.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. «The cake was partially eaten, so a big slice was still on the plate.» The clue is that a slice is still left, so the eating is not finished. Swap in the word partly: if the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: In health, partially is used with a sense, such as «partially sighted» or «partially deaf». It means a person can see or hear a little, but not everything. Partially sighted does not mean blind, and partially deaf does not mean completely deaf.
fact: Partially means partly; not completely.
fact: «Partially cooked» means not ready yet, because it still needs more cooking.
fact: «Partially sighted» means someone can see a little, but not fully.
fact: «Partially» is closely linked to the word part, so think of a piece of something.
fact: In formal writing, partially can also mean in an unfair way that favours one side, but this use is rare.
exercise: «The jug was partially filled with water.» What does partially mean here? | *Not completely | Broken into pieces | Completely, right up to the very top | Empty, with no water at all
exercise: Mia says, «The chicken is partially cooked, so it needs five more minutes.» What does partially cooked mean? | Cooked perfectly and ready to eat | *Not fully cooked yet | Burnt black on the outside | Cooked twice over
exercise: Which phrase describes someone who can see a little, but not fully? | Completely blind | *Partially sighted | Wide awake | Fully deaf
test: «The door was partially open, so the cat could slip through.» Which word could replace partially here? | *Partly | Entirely | Completely | Fully
test: Dad says, «The puddle was partially frozen, so we had to be careful.» What does this mean? | None of it was frozen at all | It was frozen, then it melted | *Some of it was frozen, but not all of it | All of it was frozen solid
exam: «Her bike was partially repaired, so Leo could only ride it slowly.» What does partially repaired mean? | Painted bright red | *Partly fixed, but not finished | Completely fixed and shiny | Thrown away
